              "description": {
                "type": "textComponent",
                "text": "(formerly St. Jude Medical, Electrophysiology Device Analyst) In this analyst role, I participated in receiving, processing, and decontaminating devices such as electrophysiology catheters, introducer sets, tubing sets, needles, or packaging complaints, while following proper decontamination procedures and protocol. This consisted of reviewing complaint and device history records (DHR) to determine an appropriate analysis plan to implement, then I systematically investigated each claim by evaluating the product through visual assessments and conduced functional tests, such as electrical testing, torque force testing, ablation simulation, EKG testing, irrigation testing, and other device-specific tests as needed. I wrote thorough evaluation reports to summarize test results and findings, as well as updated and managed the product investigation sections in the product complaint database (EPIQ), including accurate and precise entry of complaint evaluations, findings, and codes for trending issues. In addition to the analysis process, I responded to local and global requests from department directors, managers, or engineers when more information or further analysis was requested, as well as ad hoc requests for information on previous investigations or trends in product complaints. I participated in weekly cross-functional review groups and team meetings to ensure consistency and integrity, collaborate with teams to set metrics and achieve weekly goals and benchmarks, and participated in sharing complaint and report information with various cross-functional teams, collaborating on ideas and solutions such as Corrective and Preventive Actions (CAPAs), Supplier Corrective Action Request (SCARs), or Change Request (CR)."
              }
